      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Nigel Cox",
      "description": "Dartmoor: Haytor Rocks There are two main granite rock outcrops or tors at Haytor Rocks. This is the north-eastern of the pair viewed from the top of the south-western one. The height of the one in the photo is 454 metres above sea level while the one that the photographer was standing on is just 3 metres higher. There are a couple of rock climbers visible in the shot, one at the top and one at the bottom of the crag. A 49 hectare area around the tors and nearby quarries is defined as an SSSI by virtue of the geological importance of the exposures of two principal variants (the 'Giant' and 'Blue' varieties) of the coarse, megacrystic biotite-granite of Dartmoor.",
